WEBVTT

NOTE week11-clip1-forward
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.428 line:2 align:center
Diffusion models learn to generate
by learning to undo noise.

2
00:00:04.428 --> 00:00:07.349 line:2 align:center
We start from a real backbone,

3
00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:12.549 line:2 align:center
x 0, drawn here as 16 C-alpha
points in a short helix.

4
00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:15.683 line:2 align:center
Training runs in two directions.

5
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:20.254 line:2 align:center
The forward direction adds a little
Gaussian noise at every step.

6
00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:23.288 line:2 align:center
Each point drifts by a random amount,

7
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:28.083 line:2 align:center
and after the first few steps
the helix is still obvious.

8
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:33.030 line:2 align:center
You never have to take the steps
one at a time. After t steps,

9
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:39.587 line:2 align:center
x t is a single weighted mix: the square
root of the signal weight times x zero,

10
00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:45.817 line:2 align:center
plus the square root of one minus
that weight, times one Gaussian draw.

11
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:48.175 line:2 align:center
The schedule fixes those weights.

12
00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:55.498 line:2 align:center
With beta rising from 0.0001
to 0.02 over a thousand steps,

13
00:00:55.498 --> 00:01:00.201 line:2 align:center
the signal weight is 0.95 at step 100,

14
00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:07.483 line:2 align:center
0.72 at 250, and 0.28 at 500.

15
00:01:07.683 --> 00:01:14.887 line:2 align:center
By step 999 the signal weight
is 0.006: a Gaussian cloud.

16
00:01:14.887 --> 00:01:17.604 line:2 align:center
Every protein ends in the same place,

17
00:01:17.604 --> 00:01:22.350 line:2 align:center
which is exactly why sampling
can start from noise alone.

18
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:27.637 line:2 align:center
Noising needs no learning at all,
just a random number generator.

19
00:01:27.637 --> 00:01:30.061 line:2 align:center
The network only ever learns the way back.

20
00:01:30.061 --> 00:01:36.480 line:2 align:center
One real structure gives a thousand
training examples, one for every step.
